    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by using the fact that \\(\\alpha\\) is inversely proportional to \\(\\beta\\). This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{k}{\\beta}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(k\\) is a constant. We are given that \\(\\alpha = 4\\) when \\(\\beta = 9\\). Substituting these values into the equation, we find \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\n4 = \\frac{k}{9}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(k\\) by multiplying both sides by 9, we get:\n\n\\[\nk = 4 \\times 9 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow that we have determined the constant \\(k = 36\\), we can use this to find \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\). Substituting \\(\\beta = -72\\) into the equation \\(\\alpha = \\frac{k}{\\beta}\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{36}{-72}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
